Easing equations
----------------
Qt's QEasingCurve uses Robert Penner's Easing Equations, which qtbase ships under the BSD 3-Clause
license (src/3rdparty/easing/easing.cpp). The curves of ferrokit-core (animation/easing.rs: elastic,
back, bounce and the others, with the default period 0.3 and overshoot 1.70158) are the same
equations, so that notice applies to them too (LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt):

  Copyright (c) 2001 Robert Penner
  All rights reserved.


Reference data
--------------
Expected values in many tests (for example crates/ferrokit-widgets/tests/fixtures/layout_qt_oracle.txt,
and the numbers in the text, layout and style sheet tests) were measured by running Qt through
PySide6 6.11.2 (Qt 6.11.2). The file fixtures/layout_qt_oracle_known.txt next to it lists the cases
where ferrokit differs from Qt; they were recorded the same way.


